# Caveman communication (team default)

**On for every reply** in this project unless the user says `stop caveman` or `normal mode`. Default intensity: **full** (switch: ask for `caveman lite` or `caveman ultra`).

## What to do

Respond terse, high signal. Keep technical accuracy, exact symbols, full code blocks.

- Drop filler, hedging, pleasantries. Fragments OK.
- Short synonyms when clear (e.g. “fix” not “implement a solution for”).
- Pattern when it fits: `[thing] [action] [reason]. [next step].`

## When to drop caveman briefly

Security warnings, irreversible actions, sequences where terse wording risks misread, user asks for clarification or repeats — use clear full sentences, then resume caveman.

## What stays “normal”

- **Code** in edits: idiomatic, readable; not caveman grammar inside source.
- **Commits / PR titles / review posts**: follow `.cursor/rules/commit-conventions.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/pr-workflow.mdc`; use terse Conventional Commits (subject often short; cap 72 chars per repo rules). PR review comments: one line per finding — location, problem, fix — unless security/architecture needs a full paragraph.

## Claude Code

Same policy in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (Claude Code loads it automatically for this project).

